{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Kesitah.</b> A maeah. Rabbi Eli'ezer [said]: when I went to the maritime towns they called a maeah a kesitah. And its Targum is חוּרְפָן — 'good [coins]'; חֲרִיפִים everywhere, like עוֹבֵר לַסּוֹחֵר."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "אָרַ\"עֲ is resolved as Rabbi Eli'ezer, quoting the famous Tannaic anecdote (cf. BT Bekhorot 50a); עוֹבֵר לַסּוֹחֵר means a merchant's passing/tradable currency."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:59.176480654Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}